      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nThe code change is fine to land; the comments inline are minor, with no need to re-spin for them alone. One related point for a separate change: in the same caller, the encrypted-volatile path in ll_setattr_raw() calls cl_object_attr_lock(ref_lli->lli_clob) on the inode behind a user-supplied fd from volatile_ref_file(), without checking that it is a Lustre regular file or that lli_clob is non-NULL. That is pre-existing and not touched here.",
