        "subject": "LU-20923 llite: harden setattr against absent cl_object",
        "message": "LU-20923 llite: harden setattr against absent cl_object\n\ncl_setattr_ost() fetches the setattr parent FID from the inode's\ncl_object (lli_clob) and uses it to set up the setattr IO.  A regular\nfile is normally guaranteed a cl_object once CLIO setup has run, but\nnot every caller verifies this before calling.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-4-8 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ib20adee922e6690591e022ad1c275f61273ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70519\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Zhuravlev <azhuravlev@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
